WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.310
Film Courage: Harvey, you have seen so many
worlds.

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:06.259
You’ve seen the music world growing up with
your Dad, you’ve seen the basketball world,

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:10.780
advertising world, and now here in Los Angeles,
which is a totally different ball game in

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.250
many senses (no pun intended by the way).

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.519
At the risk of sounding too cliché with this,
can we talk about the dark times [in someone’s

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.260
career journey] and how you can come out of
them?

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.300
Because you’ve seen a lot, whether it is
from your own life or from other people.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.289
How do you maintain a balance, because [Los
Angeles] is a very, very up and down town?

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:34.200
Harvey Mason, Jr.: It is a very up and down
business, up and down town.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.640
You can get caught up in a lot here, specifically
in Los Angeles, about the approval of other

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.640
people.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.550
I think our whole industry is built on the
approval of other people because you don’t

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.780
get paid if other people don’t like what
you do.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.980
You are literally exposing yourself everyday
hoping other people like what you do and ultimately

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.050
hoping people they like you.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.270
That’s dangerous to a person’s psyche,
to their personality.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.690
It is almost better that we lived somewhere
else and didn’t have to deal with that.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.900
But it’s just the reality of art, right?

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.900
It’s subjective.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.760
And you’re not going to be successful if
people do not give you their approval and

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.450
say “I want to buy that record or that painting
or that sculpture or that film, whatever.”

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.210
So that’s the dangerous part.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:20.549
That is when it gets dark is when you don’t
have enough success to support your…your…not

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:27.299
ego…but just not enough support to feel
good about yourself and you start doubting

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.670
your art or your passion or “is this what
I’m supposed to be doing, maybe I shouldn’t

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.890
be doing it?”

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.310
A funny thing is, that is a part of Buster
Moon (from the movie SING).

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.710
There’s a part in the movie where he talks
about that and that’s so real and so true.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:47.330
It pertains to anybody who has ever moved
to LA to try to make music or try to be an

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.330
actress.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.470
It can test your will, it can test your dedication.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.319
A lot of people give up and they don’t make
it.

00:01:56.319 --> 00:02:02.249
I don’t have the answer on how to push through
it other than believe in yourself and continue

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:03.299
to try and improve.

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:07.819
If anybody told me that they didn't like what
I did, I took it personally and I would go

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:09.340
back to work.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.819
I would sit in my studio at the time which
was in a bedroom and I would just bang on

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:15.640
my keyboard and make another track.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.599
And then do another one….and “Nope, don’t
like it”….

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:20.069
do another one…get better…get better.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:22.470
I would really take a competitive approach
to it.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.689
I was an athlete and to me it was like “I
have to beat the next person.”

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:33.020
So rather than start doubting myself or questioning
myself, I took people at their word.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.980
It’s probably not good enough, let me get
better.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.489
And I think that served me well and I still
try to do that.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:42.990
When I’m doing a project, in the back of
my mind, there are people I’m thinking about

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:49.470
that I want to do better than and other people
who I want to hear this and I want them to

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:53.000
be mad because I did such a good job and other
people I want them to be proud that I did

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.000
such a good job.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.390
So that is definitely a constant motivation
for me.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:00.549
Film Courage: You can even see in SING that
some of them [the characters] have a few chips

00:03:00.549 --> 00:03:02.641
other shoulders and that this is not really
a bad thing.

00:03:02.641 --> 00:03:05.350
We always hear that [having a chip on one’s
shoulder] is a negative thing but it could

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.580
actually be good to have it because it’s
a driving force and if you don’t you’ll

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.580
get pummeled?

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.870
Harvey Mason, Jr: I don’t know.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.360
Different people have different ways of coping
and dealing with it.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.629
Some people make music or make art just for
themselves and they’re happy with that,

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:22.140
forget what everybody else says and I’m
just doing this because I love it.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.659
This is one way of doing it.

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:28.930
I just chose to be very competitive and I
have kids.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.189
I want my kids to be proud.

00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:32.189
I want to leave a legacy after I’m done.

00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:34.469
I want people to think I did good work.

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:38.310
I want to be able to lay down at the end and
say “Yeah.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.599
I’m happy with what I did.

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:41.719
I’m happy with what I’ve left behind.”

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:47.310
I think art is a really important part of
our culture and our society and if I can create

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.579
anything that lasts beyond my life, I think
that will be great.

00:03:51.579 --> 00:03:57.040
Not to get too philosophical but some of that
is my motivation, it’s not just about sitting

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.280
in a vacuum and making music that pleases
me.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.031
I’m trying to do things that might affect
other people in a positive way.

00:04:04.031 --> 00:04:05.031
QUESTION FOR THE VIEWERS: What motivates you,
money, achievement, personal growth, recognition

00:04:05.031 --> 00:04:05.035
or the work itself?

